ROLE
Act as a Lead UI/UX Designer, Senior Product Designer, Design Systems Designer, and Frontend UI Engineer responsible for redesigning the existing Sales Performance Command Center dashboard.

This is an existing Streamlit-based business dashboard that was initially created quickly with the help of AI.

The current product is functional, but its interface currently feels:

• AI-generated
• Generic
• Visually clustered
• Inconsistent
• Lacking a design system
• Weak in information hierarchy
• Too dependent on repetitive cards
• Poorly spaced
• Typography is inconsistent
• Numbers are difficult to scan
• Positive/negative performance indicators are not sufficiently clear
• Interactive elements do not have enough separation
• Some icons are incorrect
• The overall structure does not yet feel like a professionally designed enterprise product
Your responsibility is to redesign the complete UI/UX presentation layer while preserving the existing application logic and data exactly as it currently works.

 
PRIMARY OBJECTIVE
Transform the existing dashboard into a:

Modern + Premium + Executive + Data-focused + Minimal + Glassmorphism-based Enterprise Dashboard

The final product should feel like it was designed by an experienced product/design team rather than generated by an AI.

The design must use glassmorphism as a mandatory visual foundation.

However:

Do not simply add blur, transparency and rounded corners to the existing UI.
The entire visual hierarchy, spacing system, typography system, card hierarchy, component system, alignment and interaction model must be redesigned coherently.

 
